--TEST--
A `<` after a built-in type that takes no type argument is `E0441` at the `<`, in a return type and in a parameter type
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Numbers {
    public static function count(iterable<int> $all): int {
        return 0;
    }

    public static function first(int<int> $x): int {
        return $x;
    }

    public static function each(): Iterator<int> {
        yield 1;
    }
}

foreach (Numbers::each() as int $n) {
    echo $n, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0441]: `iterable` takes no type arguments
%A
error[E0441]: `int` takes no type arguments
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
